84","predicate":"description","object":"A flaw was found in Undertow where malformed client requests can trigger server-side stream resets without triggering abuse counters. This issue, referred to as the \"MadeYouReset\" attack, allows malicious clients to induce excessive server workload by repeatedly causing server-side stream aborts. While not a protocol bug, this highlights a common implementation weakness that can be exploited to cause a denial of service (DoS).","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a flaw was found in undertow where malformed client requests can trigger server-side stream resets without triggering abuse counters. this issue, referred to as the \"madeyoureset\" attack, allows malicious clients to induce excessive server workload by repeatedly causing server-side stream aborts. while not a protocol bug, this highlights a common implementation weakness that can be exploited to cause a denial of service (dos)."},{"subject":"CVE-2025-9784","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat build of Apache Camel 4.14.2 for Spring Boot 3.5.8","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat build of apache camel 4.14.2 for spring boot 3.5.8"},{"subject":"CVE-2025-9784","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat JBoss Enterprise Application Platform 7.1 EUS for RHEL 7","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat jboss enterprise application platform 7.1 eus for rhel 7"},{"subject":"CVE-2025-9784","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat JBoss Enterprise Application Platform 7.3 EUS for RHEL 7","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat jboss enterprise application platform 7.3 eus for rhel 7"},{"subject":"CVE-2025-9784","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat JBoss Enterprise Application Platform 7.4.24","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat jboss enterprise application platform 7.4.24"},{"subject":"CVE-2025-9784","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat JB